# Trivy accepted exceptions for the sandbox images (task C04, design/ADR-M25 §2.9). CRITICAL
# findings block the CI job `sandbox-image`. Same rules as the repo's .trivyignore: one ID per
# line, a reason, a date and Person B's approval in the pull request. Review at every upgrade of
# the OpenHands base image, and remove an entry as soon as Debian ships a fix.
#
# 2026-09-27 libxml2 in the Debian 13 base of ghcr.io/openhands/agent-server:1.48.0-python-slim;
# no fixed version released yet. Nothing in the sandbox parses untrusted XML on the platform's
# behalf. Approved by Harry (C04 session 3 plan review, PR for issue #31).
CVE-2026-6653
# 2026-09-27 linux-libc-dev (kernel headers, used only to compile native modules) in the same
# base; no fixed version released yet; a sandbox runs on the host's kernel, not these headers.
# Approved by Harry (C04 session 3 plan review, PR for issue #31).
CVE-2026-43185
# 2026-10-20 linux-libc-dev (kernel headers, used only to compile native modules) in the same
# base; no fixed version released yet; a sandbox runs on the host's kernel, not these headers
# (same reason as CVE-2026-43185). Found when PR #389 rebuilt the image. Person B approves in the
# pull request that adds them.
CVE-2026-63825
CVE-2026-93221
# 2026-10-20 linux-libc-dev, same base: Debian lists a fix (6.12.111-1), but the base image pins
# apt to a Debian snapshot of 2026-09-13 (snapshot.debian.org), which still has 6.12.107-1, so a
# build cannot install it. Same reason as above: kernel headers, the sandbox runs on the host's
# kernel. Remove when a new base image carries the fix. Person B approves in the same pull request.
CVE-2026-90037
# 2026-10-21 linux-libc-dev, same base: Debian lists a fix (6.12.113-1), but the base image's apt
# still uses the Debian snapshot of 2026-09-13 (6.12.107-1), so a build cannot install it. Same
# reason as CVE-2026-90037: kernel headers, the sandbox runs on the host's kernel. Found by the
# release-images run of v0.5.0. Remove when a new base image carries the fix. Approved by Harry
# (Person B) in the pull request that adds them.
CVE-2026-98621
CVE-2026-98725
CVE-2026-98805
# 2026-10-26 linux-libc-dev, same base: Debian lists a fix (6.12.113-1), but the base image's apt
# still uses the Debian snapshot of 2026-09-13 (6.12.107-1), so a build cannot install it. Same
# reason as CVE-2026-90037: kernel headers, the sandbox runs on the host's kernel. Found by the
# scheduled CI run of 2026-10-25 on main and by PR #445 (H05). Remove when a new base image carries
# the fix. Person B approves in the pull request that adds them.
CVE-2026-98959
CVE-2026-99078
CVE-2026-99079
# 2026-10-27 linux-libc-dev, same base: Debian lists a fix (6.12.113-1), but the base image's apt
# still uses the Debian snapshot of 2026-09-13 (6.12.107-1), so a build cannot install it. Same
# reason as CVE-2026-90037: kernel headers, the sandbox runs on the host's kernel. Found by the
# CI run of PR #451 (H02). Remove when a new base image carries the fix. Person B approves in the
# pull request that adds it.
CVE-2026-99083
# 2026-10-21 certifi 2026.6.17 in the Python of the same base: its CA bundle still holds emSign
# root CAs whose intermediate CA keys were compromised (fixed in 2026.10.19). A sandbox reaches
# only LiteLLM and the package proxy on its internal run network (ADR-M25), never a public TLS
# host, so a certificate from those CAs cannot reach it. Found by the release-images run of
# v0.5.0. Remove when a new base image carries certifi 2026.10.19 or later. Approved by Harry
# (Person B) in the pull request that adds it.
GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2
